<title>BELGIUM: GEVAERT UPS 1996 NET DIVIDEND 10 PERCENT.</title>
<headline>GEVAERT UPS 1996 NET DIVIDEND 10 PERCENT.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Twelve months to December 31,</p>
<p>1996 (in billions of Belgian francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group net profit		   4.23  vs  2.94</p>
<p>    Cons current profit		2.22  vs  1.89</p>
<p>    Cons extraordinary profit	2.06  vs  1.09</p>
<p>    Net dividend (francs)		55  vs    50</p>
<p>NOTE - Gevaert is a Belgian holding company.</p>
<p>In a statement, Gevaert said its estimated net asset value at</p>
<p>the end of 1996 was 2,700 francs per share compared with 2,245</p>
<p>francs a year earlier.</p>
<p>On February 17, the estimated net asset value was 3,007</p>
<p>francs per share, it said.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
